    "parsing_res_list": [
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Discussion Note that the total rate of heat transfer through a pipe is constant, but the heat flux  $ \\dot{q} = \\dot{Q}/(2\\pi rL) $  is not since it decreases in the direction of heat transfer with increasing radius.",
            "block_bbox": [
                95,
                106,
                1013,
                212
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "## EXAMPLE 2–16 Heat Conduction through a Spherical Shell",
            "block_bbox": [
                84,
                314,
                935,
                356
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Consider a spherical container of inner radius  $ r_{1} = 8 $  cm, outer radius  $ r_{2} = 10 $  cm, and thermal conductivity k = 45 W/m·K, as shown in Fig. 2–52. The inner and outer surfaces of the container are maintained at constant temperatures of  $ T_{1} = 200^{\\circ} $ C and  $ T_{2} = 80^{\\circ} $ C, respectively, as a result of some chemical reactions occurring inside. Obtain a general relation for the temperature distribution inside the shell under steady conditions, and determine the rate of heat loss from the container.\n\nSOLUTION A spherical container is subjected to specified temperatures on its surfaces. The variation of temperature and the rate of heat transfer are to be determined.\n\nAssumptions 1 Heat transfer is steady since there is no change with time. 2 Heat transfer is one-dimensional since there is thermal symmetry about the midpoint, and thus  $ T = T(r) $ . 3 Thermal conductivity is constant. 4 There is no heat generation.\n\nProperties The thermal conductivity is given to be k = 45 W/m·K.\n\nAnalysis The mathematical formulation of this problem can be expressed as",
            "block_bbox": [
                65,
                371,
                1015,
                605
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                45,
                634,
                1016,
                738
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                30,
                736,
                1018,
                878
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                25,
                872,
                878,
                915
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                21,
                909,
                1008,
                956
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ \\frac{d}{dr}\\left(r^{2}\\frac{dT}{dr}\\right)=0 $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                422,
                962,
                637,
                1042
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "with boundary conditions",
            "block_bbox": [
                12,
                1058,
                360,
                1095
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ \\begin{aligned}T(r_{1})&=T_{1}=200^{\\circ}C\\\\T(r_{2})&=T_{2}=80^{\\circ}C\\end{aligned} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                404,
                1102,
                664,
                1187
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Integrating the differential equation once with respect to r yields",
            "block_bbox": [
                10,
                1198,
                855,
                1244
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ r^{2}\\frac{dT}{dr}=C_{1} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                452,
                1250,
                607,
                1324
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "where  $ C_{1} $  is an arbitrary constant. We now divide both sides of this equation by  $ r^{2} $  to bring it to a readily integrable form,",
            "block_bbox": [
                8,
                1327,
                1024,
                1414
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 13
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ \\frac{dT}{dr}=\\frac{C_{1}}{r^{2}} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                469,
                1415,
                593,
                1493
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 14
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Again integrating with respect to r gives",
            "block_bbox": [
                10,
                1510,
                548,
                1549
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 15
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ T(r)=-\\frac{C_{1}}{r}+C_{2} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                410,
                1548,
                652,
                1624
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 16
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula_number",
            "block_content": "(a)",
            "block_bbox": [
                990,
                1552,
                1024,
                1582
            ],
            "block_id": 16,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "We now apply both boundary conditions by replacing all occurrences of r and  $ T(r) $  in the relation above by the specified values at the boundaries. We get",
            "block_bbox": [
                11,
                1618,
                1028,
                1723
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
            "block_order": 17
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ T(r_{1})=T_{1}\\quad\\rightarrow\\quad-\\frac{C_{1}}{r_{1}}+C_{2}=T_{1} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                312,
                1726,
                754,
                1812
            ],
            "block_id": 18,
            "block_order": 18
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ T(r_{2})=T_{2}\\quad\\rightarrow\\quad-\\frac{C_{1}}{r_{2}}+C_{2}=T_{2} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                317,
                1826,
                756,
                1908
            ],
            "block_id": 19,
            "block_order": 19
        },
        {
            "block_label": "image",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"imgs/img_in_image_box_1187_387_1585_659.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" width=\"24%\" /></div>\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                1187,
                387,
                1585,
                659
            ],
            "block_id": 20,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">FIGURE 2–52</div>\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                1399,
                672,
                1597,
                710
            ],
            "block_id": 21,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Schematic for Example 2–16.</div>\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                1186,
                711,
                1601,
                757
            ],
            "block_id": 22,
            "block_order": null
        }
    ],
